\par\par \b \uc2  REPEAT: \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervening \highlight\uc2  In Money Market \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2001\par 18:04\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the money market Thursday, selling dollars for the second time in the week to bolster the sol, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said. \par \par \uc2  At 1530 GMT the nuevo sol was trading at PEN3.5910 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.5900 to PEN 3.5920. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol had reached levels of PEN3.5950 to the dollar in early morning trade on local electoral worries and regional instability led by Argentina, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol had closed Wednesday at a mid-rate of PEN3.5910 a dollar. "We just entered in the market and we will continue there," an official said, declining to give a maximum amount of dollars to be sold. Local traders pegged the amount at about $3 million. Peru's local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weakened notably after the first round of presidential elections held April 8. No candidate took the majority, and a second round of voting will likely be held in early June. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official report on Wednesday monetary and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it sold $17.5 million Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Managing Director Javier de la Rocha said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't have an exchange rate target, local newspaper Gestion reported Thursday. \par \par \uc2  De la Rocha said if there is a high volatility in the market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to calm investors' nervousness. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  officially has a "dirty float" and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps a tight hold on liquidity. \par \par \uc2  The sol's recent depreciation is due to Argentina's situation and the uncertainty related to Peru's electoral process, authorities had said. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Javier Silva Ruete agreed with Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Gestion reported Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Silva Ruete said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "necessary" and it is a 'normal instrument.' \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Before Wednesday, the last time that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold dollars was\par in November 1999.\par -By Virginia Rey-Sanchez, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050;\par peru@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010710dx4q00m7p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
