\par\par \b \uc2  Peru cenbank says will sell dollars to defend sol. \b0\par\par\uc2 132 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 April 2001\par 17:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LIMA, Peru, April 25 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to sell dollars after the sol \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  PEN=) fell to a historic low through the psychological barrier of 3.6 to the dollar on jitters about Peru's upcoming elections and the crisis in Argentina. \par \par \uc2  "We are going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's falls," a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official told Reuters, giving no details. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The bank has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets since March 3, 2000. \par \par \uc2  The sol \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at 3.590/5950 per dollar on Wednesday morning at 10:17 local time (1517 GMT) after opening at 3.594/3.6050. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4p01d7r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
