\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2 's Sol Ends Stronger After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 April 2001\par 21:51\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's nuevo sol ended stronger Wednesday as the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by selling dollars seeking to curb a dollar-purchase rally by investors, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed at a midrate of PEN3.5910 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.5905-PEN3.5915 per dollar, local traders said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol had closed the day before at a midrate of PEN3.5950 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.5940-PEN3.5960 per dollar, local traders said. \par \par \uc2  "Investors were buying dollars due to investor concerns on Argentina's economy and the local political environment but the sol strengthened when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars," a trader at Banco de Credito said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will release the dollar amount sold late Wednesday but an official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was "close to $15 million." \par \par \uc2  The last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars was November 1999. \par \par \uc2  The sol weakened to PEN3.6055 at one point in trading. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, Peru's authorities said it was possible that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could sell dollars on the market. \par \par \uc2  Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has been shaken by political uncertainty ahead of a presidential run-off election likely to be held in early June. \par \par \uc2  Traders also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered PEN300 million in overnight repurchase agreements, or repos but it only placed PEN297 million at an average rate of 11.67%. \par \par \uc2  The key overnight lending rate in soles as of April 24 was 12.81%. \par \par \uc2  As of April 24, the outstanding value of CDs, used by the government to control the money supply and influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was PEN1.865 billion, same as the day before. \par \par \uc2  -Virginia Rey-Sanchez, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010711dx4p00396\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
