\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2 's Ctrl Bk Chief Says  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Possible \b0\par\par\uc2 438 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 2001\par 22:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  LIMA -(Dow Jones)- The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if conditions make it necessary, the general manager of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Javier de la Rocha, said Friday. \par \par \uc2  De la Rocha said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would hold a meeting late Friday with representatives of local banks to discuss market jitters, including a sharp increase in interbank lending rates. \par \par \uc2  "There is really no reason for the interbank interest rate to be at about 16%. That is what is worrying us," de la Rocha said. "That interest rate is pure nervousness." \par \par \uc2  Thursday's interbank exchange rate reached 15.72% from 12.59% on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  De la Rocha added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't shy away from using the market mechanisms available to it. \par \par \uc2  "We are going to call them to talk things over, calm them down, and make them see that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  obviously holds certain instruments and that will have to be used if to the extent that it is necessary. But of course not in excess," de la Rocha told reporters. \par \par \uc2  No specific trigger rates for the interbank interest rate nor the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate have been fixed, he added. Nevertheless, the absence of transactions could be an indicator for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. \par \par \uc2  "We say our floating exchange rate is 'dirty' because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any moment despite the fact that it has been two years since we have sold (U.S. dollars) and one year since we have bought them," he said. \par \par \uc2  De la Rocha dismissed sharp exchange rate fluctuations this week in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  citing similar volatility in Brazil, Chile, and Mexico and Peru's upcoming run-off elections. \par \par \uc2  "I don't see anything unusual in all this," he said. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has been shaken by political uncertainty ahead of the presidential run-off election to be held May 27 or June 3. \par \par \uc2  Peru's nuevo sol firmed Friday to PEN3.5700 amid tight liquidity in soles after sliding down to PEN3.5813 per dollar Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Separately, de la Rocha said the change in  Argentina's exchange rate convertibility scheme wouldn't affect the Peruvian market. \par \par \uc2  The bank official also remarked that proposals by presidential candidates to lower minimum reserve requirements for dollar denominated bank deposits, or to change over to a referential interest rate scheme wouldn't have significant impact in the short term. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I say if something is working, why change it?" de la Rocha said.\par -By Miriam Gerace, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx4k01s4u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
