\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2  Sol Ends Stronger Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 217 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 1999\par 21:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's nuevo sol finished stronger Tuesday despite a round of dollar purchases by the Central Reserve Bank of Peru for a second consecutive day, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol closed at a mid-rate of PEN3.3265 per dollar on a spread of PEN3.325-PEN3.328 per dollar, local traders said. \par \par \uc2  That is stronger than Monday's close at PEN3.3318 on a spread of PEN3.3300-PEN3.3335 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The sol strengthened despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggressive dollar purchases for second consecutive day, as neither banks nor companies seemed to be interested in buying dollars," said a trader at Banco de Credito. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $23.6 million, in what one official said was a move to copy what most private banks aim to do - buy cheap and sell higher. \par \par \uc2  The key overnight lending rate was around 9.0%, traders said, lower than Monday's official closing figure at 11.0%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As of May 3, the outstanding value of CDs, used by the government to\par control the money supply and influence the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was PEN 329.9\par million.\par   -By Virginia Rey-Sanchez; 511-221-7050;VReySanchez@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 04-05-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1921GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv5403fq6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscal