\par\par \b \uc2  Peru Banks Push Plan For New Aid Program \b0\par\par\uc2 203 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 23:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's troubled banks need a state-run program that will help keep them above water, Mario Ferrari, the director of the national banking association, Asbanc, said Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The fund will serve to help keep afloat troubled banks that the government has decided to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in," he said before a committee of Congress. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's banks have been hard hit by a downturn in economic activity, particularly as many of their loans are denominated in U.S. dollars, which has strengthened against the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The proposed fund should be administrated not only by the Superintendency of Banking and Insurance but also by the finance ministry and the Central Reserve Bank of Peru, said Enrique Arroyo, another banking association official speaking at the same committee session. \par \par \uc2  The private banking official said they want the new fund to complement the existing deposit insurance fund, which they fund themselves. \par \par \uc2  Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president German Suarez told the committee that the deposit insurance fund has grown to reach $100 million. \par \par \uc2  That fund only covers deposits up to a value of 62,822 soles ($1=PEN3.376). \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 22-03-99 \par \par \uc2  2231GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv3m029di\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
