\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2  Sol Ends Down Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 1999\par 22:22\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  LIMA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's nuevo sol (PEN) finished weaker against the U.S. dollar Wednesday, as banks and companies continue to buy dollars despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  According to local traders, the sol ended trading at mid rate of PEN3.4000 a dollar on a spread of PEN3.3970-3.4000/dollar, compared to Tuesday's close at PEN3.3860 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.3900-PEN3.3820/ dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Banks and companies were buying dollars, but it seems than many \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  were speculative," said a trader at Banco de Credito. He added investors remain a bit nervous following Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation last month. \par \par \uc2  Market participants are also watching closely Peru's current account deficit, estimated to have reached 6.4% of gross domestic product at the end of 1998 - still high for regional standards. \par \par \uc2  The Central Reserve Bank Of Peru sold $20 million. Finance minister and other government officials have said the government wouldn't hesitate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market against speculators. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not acted in the market since Jan. 13, when it sold $10.5 million. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also sold PEN46.6 million in four-week certificates of deposit, which gave some support to the sol. \par \par \uc2  The key interbank interest rate stood around 18.0% Wednesday, down from Tuesday's 18.6%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the informal market, the dollar traded at PEN3.42 to the dollar,\par weaker than Tuesday's PEN3.39.\par -By Virginia Rey-Sanchez; 511-221-7050; VReySanchez@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  03-02-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2122GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1071 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010827dv230010s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
