\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk/Defend Sol -2: No  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Expected \b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 1998\par 19:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA (Dow Jones)--The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  will consider selling dollars to defend the nuevo sol (PEN) if the sol appears to weaken "irrationally," \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President German Suarez said Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Suarez, speaking in Congress, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to defend the sol in recent months. He also said that he didn't expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken irrationally. \par \par \uc2  "Indications are that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will trade within acceptable limits," Suarez said. \par \par \uc2  Suarez said he didn't expect the Colombian peso's devaluation to hurt the sol significantly, since the situations in the countries were different. \par \par \uc2  "This is a very different economy," Suarez said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that despite Colombia's problems, the sol should gain against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The sol should actually strengthen in the coming sessions, since the supply of dollars is relatively high," a local analyst said. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the sol weakened slightly in early trading Wednesday. But, despite a devaluation of Colombia's peso, the sol was rallying late in the session. \par \par \uc2  The analysts said that the sol was being helped by PEN62 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  certificates of deposit maturing Wednesday. Additionally, the Lima Stock Exchange is showing gains Wednesday, something that normally helps the sol. \par \par \uc2  In recent trading, the sol was trading at PEN3.0452, about the same as Tuesday's close at PEN3.0450. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (The original item, "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Peru\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Ctrl Bk/Defend Sol -2: No \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par Expected," timed about 1713 GMT, attributed some of the analysts\par comments to Suarez.)\par -By Eric J. Lyman and Virginia Rey-Sanchez; 511-221-7050\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 02-09-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1713GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Corrected 1927GMT)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9207jop\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
