\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2  Nuevo Sol Weakend Sharply, Rumors Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 157 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 1997\par 23:28\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's nuevo sol weakened sharply in moderate trading Thursday, as traders said unconfirmed rumors of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hurt the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The sol ended the day at 2.655 per dollar, compared to 2.648 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on the rumors, but traders said they effected the exchange rate, which saw the sol strengthen in five of the last seven sessions. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange rate, usually acting to weaken the sol as part of its strategy to make exports more attractive and narrow the country's $1.94 billion trade deficit. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The sol also weakened in street trading - the price the sol trades\par informally - falling to 2.64 per dollar from 2.63 per dollar.\par    -Eric J. Lyman\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT  21-08-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2128GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1071 1802 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011006dt8l00b14\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
