\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2  Nuevo Sol Weaker;Media Reports On Proposed  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 1997\par 22:49\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's nuevo sol weakened slightly Tuesday, but volume was low despite local media reports that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be preparing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The sol weakened to 2.656 per dollar after closing at 2.654 per dollar in each of the last three sessions. \par \par \uc2  The media reports on \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity seemed to have little effect on the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  The financial daily Gestion reported that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be buying dollars in coming weeks to help raise $800 million to pay off foreign debt. As reported, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a five-year high of $425 million in dollars in June, and indications are that it is buying dollars at nearly the same pace so far in July. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on the report. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the financial daily Sintesis reported that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was considering a mild devaluation of the sol. Again, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment, but analysts dismissed the move as unlikely. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The sol was unchanged in street trading - the price the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sells\par for informally - trading at 2.63 per dollar.\par    -Eric J. Lyma