\par\par \b \uc2  Peru Sol Stronger At Mid-Session Due To Low Inflation \b0\par\par\uc2 133 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 17:24\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's nuevo sol strengthened 0.6% against the dollar in the first two hours of trading Tuesday, with traders citing the low inflation rate in February for increased demand. \par \par \uc2  The sol traditionally weakens slightly faster than the rate of inflation due mostly to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Traders said the low inflation rate for February, announced Monday, prompted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators to buy soles. \par \par \uc2  Peru's February inflation rate was 0.09%, the lowest one-month total in Peru since June 1973. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Around 1400 GMT, the sol was trading at 2.630 per dollar after opening\par at 2.645 per dollar.\par    -Eric J. Lyman\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 04-03-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1624GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1071 1802 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011006dt34005b2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
