\par\par \b \uc2  Peru Sol Stronger At Mid-Session Due To Low Inflation \b0\par\par\uc2 137 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 23:01\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's nuevo sol strengthened against the dollar Tuesday as traders said low inflation in February increased demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The sol ended the day at 2.637 per dollar, compared to 2.645 per dollar Monday. The sol had traded as strong as 2.630 per dollar at mid-session. \par \par \uc2  The sol traditionally weakens slightly faster than the rate of inflation due mostly to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Traders said the low inflation rate for February, announced Monday, prompted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators to buy soles. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Peru's February inflation rate was 0.09%, the lowest one-month total\par in Peru since June 1973.\par    -Eric J. Lyman\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 04-03-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2201GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1071 1802 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011006dt34001l8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
