\par\par \b \uc2  Exotic  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2 / \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2  -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Interventions \highlight\uc2  Ebb \b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 1996\par 19:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The recent slide in the value of the sol has made finance ministry year-end predictions for the sol, normally considered somewhat unrealistic, now seem conservative. \par \par \uc2  In January, the ministry said the year would end with the sol trading at 2.60 per dollar, while most brokerage houses at the time predicted about 2.58 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The finance ministry hasn't changed its prediction, but brokerage houses such as Flemming's Investment Bank, Interfip Bolsa, Peruval, Hildebrandt and Ferrar and Santander are now predicting a year-end rate in the 2.63-sol to 2.65-sol range. \par \par \uc2  So far in the fourth quarter, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold only about $8 million worth of soles, mainly to meet standard obligations and not to dampen the sol. \par \par \uc2  That's in considerable contrast to the first three quarters of the year when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to its own figures, sold soles for $979.8 million. During that period, the sol weakened to 2.512 sols per dollar from 2.330 sols per dollar. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the nuevo sol weakened slightly to close at 2.591 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  And with the stock market showing little promise of rebounding soon, analysts expect that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't be necessary for most of the rest of this year. \par \par \uc2  'Other forces are weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' said Lima economist Jorge Gomes, a former finance ministry official, referring to the declining stock exchange. 'There's no reason for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in when what they would have happen is happening naturally.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-11-96 \par \par \uc2  1826GMT \par \par \uc2  1106 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dsb700osf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
