\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2  Sol Weakens, Prompting New  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Rumors \b0\par\par\uc2 196 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 1996\par 23:32\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA (Dow Jones)--The nuevo sol weakened substantially against the dollar Thursday, as demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slackened with low volume on the stock exchange after Tuesday's holiday, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar strengthened to 2.566 nuevo sols after closing at 2.545 nuevo sols Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday was the Virgin of the Rosary day in Peru, a market holiday. Analysts said the sol reached another all-time low against the dollar because of low demand as investors stayed away because of the short week. \par \par \uc2  The quickness of the sols weakening prompted some analysts to suggest that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might again be buying dollars to erode the value of the sol. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the sol periodically as part of its strategy to make Peruvian exports more attractive and help curb the country's $2.14 billion trade deficit. \par \par \uc2  The nuevo sol also weakened in street trading, the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  based on what it trades for informally, trading at 2.53 per dollar after trading at 2.52 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 10-10-96 \par \par \uc2  2132GMT \par \par \uc2  1802 1837 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011013dsaa00in8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
