\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Plans  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  To Weaken Sol: Report \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 1996\par 17:14\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Peru plans to spend about $16 million a week to buy dollars on the open market and contain a recent rebound of the nuevo sol, the financial daily Gestion reported Wednesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders acknowledged Wednesday that new rumors about the planned government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market have been circulating, but haven't been confirmed. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials weren't immediately available to comment on the report. \par \par \uc2  During April and May the government was rumored to have spent as much as $70 million \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to erode the nuevo sol and curb the country's problematic trade deficit which hit $2.68 billion at the end of May. \par \par \uc2  That \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action helped to drive the dollar up to 2.455 nuevo sols last week from 2.333 nuevo sols in mid-April. \par \par \uc2  But since last Wednesday, the nuevo sol has gained against the dollar four days out of five, creeping back up to 2.442 nuevo sols. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In its letter of intent to the International Monetary Fund (IMF)\par signed last month, Peru said the nuevo sol would trade at about 2.65\par nuevo sols per dollar by year's end, which would show a slight net\par depreciation against the dollar when adjusted for anticipated 1996\par inflation of about 11.5%.\par    -Eric J. Lyman\par \f2