\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2  Central Bk Declines Comment On Sol  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Reports \b0\par\par\uc2 165 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 1996\par 17:54\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  LIMA (DJ-EMR)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined Wednesday to comment on reports it has been buying soles over the last three months to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from dropping in value against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Radio Programas reported Wednesday, citing two unnamed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has maintained \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying activity since mid-November. \par \par \uc2  But a spokesperson for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to confirm or deny the report, saying it was against policy to discuss the bank's financial activities. \par \par \uc2  The sol, Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1993, dropped sharply in value last October and November. During a five-week span in those two months, the dollar rose to 2.345 soles from 2.222 soles, setting nine all-time highs en route. \par \par \uc2  But since then, the Peruvian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stabilized and the dollar was trading at 2.325 soles Wednesday morning. \par \par \uc2  --Eric J. Lyman \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 01-24-96 \par \par \uc2  1154EST \par \par \uc2  1802 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011013ds1o003cm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
